Z||000002||BOILERMAKER||04-04-2000||12:09 PM||||I just recently acquired a free SE (86 I think) with the dual pipes on it and it was a 4 banger also.  My father said that one other time he also acquired a car that was a 4 with the dual pipes, so I know you are the only one, but don't know which models they put them on.||||reg||1
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||04-04-2000||12:40 PM||||As I understand it, the SE in 85 and 86 (Im not sure about 87) was the option model. You could have it fully loaded and have it as a 4 cyl. The SE was the only model where the V6 was an option. The GTs of course had the V6 standard. I ran into one of these SE when I was looking for a Fiero for my wife.<P>BTW to get rid of the duplicate you can click on to the "edit" icon above the message and it gives you a delete option.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||04-04-2000||01:42 PM||||Yep, the 86 and 87 SE's had the 4 bangers with dual outlets.  Don't know if it was an option or standard equipment.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||SCCA FIERO||04-04-2000||02:12 PM||||Are you sure 86 SEs came with 4 cylinders? I have never seen an 86SE with one, but have seen many 87s with 4 cylinders. And all 87s that I have seen with 4 cylindes did have the dual exhaust. Somebody help me out here. I thought I knew everything... this can't be happening.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||04-04-2000||03:28 PM||||86 and 87 SE's came equipped with the 4, with the V6 as an option.  Let me find the build numbers for the 4 cyl...<BR>there were 4,031 86 SE 4cyl, compared to 28,274 with the v6, in 87 there were 3,875 with the 4, while there were only 3,135 SE's with the 6cyl.  that could explain why you saw lots of 87's with the duke, but no 86's.<BR>go to <A HREF="http://www.fiero.mn.org/Knowledge/Features/Fieroproduction.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.mn.org/Knowledge/Features/Fieroproduction.htm</A>  for all the numbers||||reg||1
Z||000007||DRH||04-04-2000||03:38 PM||||SCCA - according to the site below, the 86 SE V6 outnumbered the 86 SE 4 by about 7 to 1. Could explain why you haven't seen one yet.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I don't know about the exhaust although I have seen/heard some SE 4s with duals. How could someone tell them apart without popping the decklid or listening ???<P><BR>*** Duh... forgot the URL ***<BR> <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~paulv/Price%20Guide.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~paulv/Price%20Guide.htm</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by DRH (edited 04-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||DRH||04-04-2000||03:47 PM||||Hey Standard, you beat me too it.<P>The numbers look pretty close except for the 87 SEs. Wonder which is right there? The one I posted has the number of sport coupe 4 cyl matching the count on your's for SE V6.<P>Otherwise they seem to match pretty close. Looks like they made the Meras from GTs in 87 and Formulas in 88. ||||reg||1
