Z||000014||Eric||04-05-2000||10:00 PM||||Hey Chadman, are you serious about the AutoX?  It would be nice to have another Fiero there to compare times with.  The first "fun" event is Sunday, April 30 at Delphi parking lot I believe.  Email me if you intend to go and I'll tell you what you need to do and bring.<P>As far as modifying your car is concerned, I don't think the tech inspectors would ever notice if you had a dual looking exhaust if it looked somewhat stock.  I had several mods done to my car which really didn't do much to increase performace, much like a dual tipped exhaust, and the tech inspectors never looked twice.  There was one guy with a brand new Miata and he got busted for having a k&n cone filter and a strut tower brace, so I guess it depends how obvious the mods are.  Chad, you'd better make sure they don't see that turbo muffler in place of the cat.  I don't know how they could say you had an unfair advantage by having it, but they can be quite crafty.  As for me, I'll take off all my performance stickers including the GM Performace Parts on my center consul (it may raise a few eyebrows) and I'll paint my MSD coil.  And the most important part, don't wash the car before you bring it.||||reg||1
Z||000015||ChadMan||04-06-2000||08:36 AM||||Serious as a "hat attack" (Boston pronunciation).  We're flying back from AZ April 29, so I should be able to make an autocross April 30 if it's in Columbus (Delphi is on the West Side, right?).  I'll email you today, Eric!||||reg||1
